# 2025-10-09 01:44:00.656644
+Please make the following changes:
+
+GOALS
+- Add a new script: scripts/chunk_and_ingest.py that chunks long articles, extracts IOCs/entities, creates rich payloads, and upserts to Qdrant.
+- Enhance api/search_api_rich.py so /search returns the full payload (not just text/tokens) and supports simple filters.
+- Keep existing /health and /version as-is.
+- Ensure requirements.txt includes sentence-transformers.
+
+DETAILS
+
+A) New file: scripts/chunk_and_ingest.py
+- CLI usage:
+  python scripts/chunk_and_ingest.py --src combined.json --collection ${QDRANT_COLLECTION:-heva_docs} --qdrant-url ${QDRANT_URL:-http://localhost:6333} --max-chars 1200 --overlap 150
+- Behavior:
+  1) Load JSON or JSONL (array or line-delimited) from --src.
+  2) For each record, chunk the "text" field with soft sentence boundaries (approx 1200 chars, 150 char overlap).
+  3) For each doc, extract:
+     - cves: CVE-\d{4}-\d{4,7}
+     - ips: IPv4s
+     - domains: basic domain regex
+     - hashes: hex 32..64
+     - mitre techniques: T\d{4}(\.\d{3})?
+     - simple actor/malware mentions (TA402, APT-C-23, IronWind, NimbleMamba, SharpSploit), case-insensitive
+  4) Build a rich payload per chunk with (at minimum):
+     {
+       "doc_id", "chunk_id", "chunk_index", "chunk_total",
+       "offset_start", "offset_end",
+       "source_url", "source_type", "title", "authors",
+       "published_at", "harvested_at", "language",
+       "text", "char_count",
+       "ioc": {"cves", "ips", "domains", "hashes"},
+       "entities": [],  // pass-through from source if present
+       "attacks": {"actors", "malware", "mitre_techniques"},
+       "tags": ["source:combined.json"] + (source tags if present),
+       "queries": up to 5 strings (title/snippet/first IOCs),
+       "emb_model": "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
+       "emb_dim": 384,
+       "neighborhood": {"prev_chunk_id", "next_chunk_id"},
+       "scoring": {"risk_score": null, "confidence": null},
+       "eval": {}, "fingerprint": "md5:<hex>", "acl": ["public"]
+     }
+  5) Encode chunk text with all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and upsert in batches of ~500 to Qdrant.
+  6) Print a summary: number of docs and chunks ingested.
+
+- Also include a helper function that (optionally) creates indexes for fields commonly filtered:
+  - tags (KEYWORD), ioc.cves (KEYWORD), attacks.actors (KEYWORD)
+  - optional text index for "text" with WORD tokenizer
+  - This function should be callable with --create-indexes flag.
+
+B) Update api/search_api_rich.py
+- Keep /health and /version unchanged.
+- Modify /search to:
+  1) Accept query params:
+     - query (str, required), limit (int, default 5)
+     - min_score (float, default 0)  // post-filter client-side after search
+     - tags (str, optional, comma-separated, e.g. "source:combined.json,topic:phishing")
+     - source_type (str, optional)
+     - doc_id (str, optional)
+     - after (RFC3339 date string), before (RFC3339), optional
+     - has_ioc (bool, optional) -> requires at least one IOC list non-empty
+  2) Build a Qdrant filter (must/should) on:
+     - payload.tags contains all requested tags (if provided)
+     - payload.source_type equals source_type (if provided)
+     - payload.doc_id equals doc_id (if provided)
+     - payload.published_at >= after / <= before (if provided and parsable)
+     - has_ioc == true => ("ioc.cves" non-empty OR "ioc.ips" non-empty OR "ioc.domains" non-empty OR "ioc.hashes" non-empty)
+  3) Perform vector search using the same model as ingestion (all-MiniLM-L6-v2).
+  4) Return results as:
+     {
+       "query": "...",
+       "results": [
+         {
+           "score": <float>,
+           "payload": <the full Qdrant payload object, unchanged>,
+           "id": <point id>
+         },
+         ...
+       ]
+     }
+  5) If min_score is set, filter out results with score < min_score.
+  6) Do not break existing behavior for simple calls with just query+limit.
+
+C) requirements.txt
+- Ensure it contains:
+  fastapi
+  uvicorn[standard]
+  qdrant-client
+  pydantic>=2
+  httpx
+  pytest
+  ruff
+  sentence-transformers
+
+TESTS / ACCEPTANCE
+- After building:
+  1) Ingest: `python scripts/chunk_and_ingest.py --src combined.json --create-indexes`
+  2) API up: `uvicorn api.search_api_rich:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`
+  3) `curl :8000/health` -> {"status":"ok"}
+  4) `curl ":8000/search?query=IronWind%20phishing&limit=3"` returns items with a "payload" object and "score".
+  5) `curl ":8000/search?query=CVE-2023-1234&has_ioc=true&limit=3"` returns chunks whose payload.ioc.cves includes "cve-2023-1234" (case-insensitive compare ok).
+  6) `curl ":8000/search?query=phishing&tags=source:combined.json&min_score=0.5&limit=3"` includes only payloads having that tag and score >= 0.5.
+
+Please implement with careful error handling and concise logging.
+

